I don't think that this is completely right.  From what I observed, I 
believe that a lycanthrope in its wereform will *always* change back to 
human when its hit points would go to zero otherwise.  When it is in 
human form, it can be killed for good.  However, the frequency of 
changing from the human to the wereform, is quite high (at least when 
you play a lycanthrope yourself, it seems you can hardly ever keep him 
human for any extended period of time).

I think the "solution" to Janis's problem is - provided his character is 
strong enough, to keep killing the werecreature.  Since it loses power 
points each time changing form, it will eventually be incapable of 
changing form again.  (I think the message then is "the werecreature 
shudders", and it will die, even if in wereform.)  When my werewolf 
first met a vampire, he was pissed off by the fact that vampires are so 
strong in slash'em but then realized that he could fight him for quite 
some time, by polymorphing back into wereform each time after having 
been reduced to human form.  That strategy was ended by a lack in energy...
